# Next.js (App Router, 15+) + Supabase

## Next.js
- Use the App Router (`app/`). Never create `pages/` routes or use `getServerSideProps` / `getStaticProps`.
- Components are Server Components by default. Add `"use client"` only for state, effects, event handlers or browser APIs, and push it to the smallest leaf component.
- Fetch data in Server Components or Route Handlers, not in `useEffect`.
- Mutations: Server Actions (`"use server"`) with input validated by zod. Call `revalidatePath`/`revalidateTag` after writes.
- In Next.js 15+, `params`, `searchParams`, `cookies()` and `headers()` are async: `const { id } = await params`.
- Only `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` env vars reach the browser. Never prefix a secret with it.

## Supabase
- Use `@supabase/ssr` (`createServerClient` / `createBrowserClient`). `@supabase/auth-helpers-nextjs` is deprecated; never import it.
- Keep two factories: `utils/supabase/server.ts` (cookies-based, for Server Components/Actions/Route Handlers) and `utils/supabase/client.ts` (browser). Refresh the session in `middleware.ts` (renamed `proxy.ts` in Next.js 16; use whichever your version expects).
- On the server, authorise with `supabase.auth.getUser()` (verifies the JWT), not `getSession()` (reads unverified cookie data).
- Row Level Security is ON for every table in `public`. Every new table ships with a migration that enables RLS and adds policies, e.g. `using ((select auth.uid()) = user_id)`.
- The service-role key is server-only, never in client code or `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, and only for admin tasks that must bypass RLS.
- Schema changes go in `supabase/migrations/*.sql` via `supabase migration new`; never edit the remote DB by hand. Regenerate types with `supabase gen types typescript` and use the `Database` type in clients.
- Always check `{ data, error }`; throw or return a typed error, never ignore `error`.

## Example
```ts
// app/notes/page.tsx (Server Component)
import { createClient } from "@/utils/supabase/server";
import { redirect } from "next/navigation";

export default async function NotesPage() {
  const supabase = await createClient();
  const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser();
  if (!user) redirect("/login");
  const { data: notes, error } = await supabase.from("notes").select("id, title").order("created_at", { ascending: false });
  if (error) throw error;
  return <ul>{notes.map((n) => <li key={n.id}>{n.title}</li>)}</ul>;
}
```
